## THE TICKETS, THE AUTHORITY, AND WHAT THIS KIT DOES NOT DO
- **RD-455** (size M in the sweep's row; labels `operations`, `s61`, `security`). Its defect (as reported, re-measured by the drafter at main by plain node, section FOUND 1): a SCIM save with no token returns HTTP 400 `INVALID_SCIM_TOKEN` because the validator rejects a body whose `scimBearerToken` is shorter than `MIN_SCIM_TOKEN_LENGTH` (32) before the route's keep-the-stored-token step can run; the panel never holds the stored token (the GET returns only `scimTokenConfigured`), so every mapping edit forced a new token. Its acceptance criteria, quoted: "1. Decide and record whether an omitted token in mode scim means 'keep the stored token' (as the persist comment intends). This touches the SCIM credential path, so the change gets a security review." "2. If kept: a mapping-only Save with a stored token succeeds and the stored token is unchanged (byte-equal before/after); a Save with no stored token and no submitted token is still refused with an explanation." "3. Cells red at origin/main, green at head; tier-1 gate (security-relevant)." **This kit builds the "kept" branch, with ONE narrowing that is the coordinator's default (Q-3): keep applies only when the stored mode is ALREADY scim and a token is stored.** A switch into scim from off or graph with a token left over from an earlier period still requires a new token (the persist step never clears a token on a mode change, so without the narrowing a mode press would silently re-arm an old credential). The drafter measured both ways (FOUND 1: the unnarrowed variant, mutation `455-keep-any-mode`, makes a save from `off` to `scim` with no token return 200). **Not done:** the panel's wording for a kept token (the save note still tells the admin to paste the token into Entra; LEFT FOR OTHERS 2), and any change to `static/**` (the panel already omits the token unless one was just generated: `static/js/entra-provisioning-ui.js` lines 1309 and 1321 at the drafting main, printed by `grep -n` over the tarball copy).
- **RD-728** is **EXCLUDED (a card, not a build)**. Its text (quoted): "add MACHINE_ID, WEBSITE_SITE_NAME and LEGACY_MACHINE_IDS to the cell's scrub list (restored after) ... plus reword 'read through this module only'", "Where: __tests__/rd628-two-machine-id-derivations.test.js ... and the header comment in backend/encryptionService.js, on rd-628-two-machine-id-derivations-s86m (a5799f3)". **Measured: neither target exists at main.** `__tests__/rd628-two-machine-id-derivations.test.js` is not in main's tree (`gh api -X GET .../contents/__tests__/rd628-two-machine-id-derivations.test.js?ref=<main>` answers `Not Found`; control: the same read of `backend/encryptionService.js` prints its blob `31fd8a4d5b716eadc9d157bef9c2019119f3b683`), and the phrase `through this module only` has count 0 in main's `backend/encryptionService.js` (control: `machine-id` counts 16 in the same file). The branch `rd-628-two-machine-id-derivations-s86m` is one commit ahead of an old base and 917 behind main (`compare` status `diverged`), touching `__tests__/rd628-two-machine-id-derivations.test.js`, `backend/encryptionService.js` and the counts file; RD-628 is in Testing. **So RD-728 is a follow-up to a change that is not on main; it becomes buildable when RD-628's branch lands (and the comment fix needs the same file).** Appending it to another seat's branch is never this kit's. **Where it stays tracked:** RD-728 itself (To Do), after RD-628 lands (LEFT FOR OTHERS 1).
- **RD-981** (Medium; labels `b1363-2026-11-07`, `b1434-2026-11-10`). Its recommendation, quoted: "first make a cell that is red on today's file for a long list with a null first row, run enough trials to see the leak (the review saw 1 to 3 in 20), then make sure no INSERT of a failed list can run after the ROLLBACK. One shape that could do that, not measured: send the INSERTs one after another so none is queued behind a failure, or send one multi-row statement. The ticket needs an independent review and a decision on whether any caller of this method reaches production". **This kit builds the first shape (Q-4: sequential INSERTs; the multi-row statement is the alternative, not taken because a long list can exceed SQLite's bound-variable limit and because the sequential shape changes nothing about row order or ids).** **The production-caller question, answered by the drafter at main (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, `grep -c -i` over the tarball copy with controls): `backend/server.js` holds `setQuickQuestions` once (count 1), and that one hit is `jsonStorage.setQuickQuestions` (count 1; `database.setQuickQuestions` and `simpleDb.setQuickQuestions` count 0; control: `database = new SimpleDatabase` counts 2 in the same file, so the server does construct the store); the files under `backend`, `scripts` and `static` that name the method are `backend/jsonStorage.js`, `backend/server.js` and `backend/simpleDb.js` only; the tests that call the simpleDb method are `__tests__/rd913-archiver-sqlite3-characterisation.test.js` (cell S4) and `__tests__/rd973-simpledb-rollback-before-reject.test.js`.** So **no production caller of the simpleDb method was found** (a text search: dynamic dispatch is a named limit); the fix is hardening of a method only tests reach, and the ticket's own "a decision on whether any caller reaches production" is recorded here as the coordinator's reading, not a ruling. **Not done:** the rate of the real race inside a jest worker (Q-5: no trial loop is a gate; the