## WHAT THE DRAFTER FOUND (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER; NO JEST WAS RUN; the instrument is `node` v24.22.2 plain scripts and `git`, in the drafter's scratch folder `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/state/s332/d2139/`; a tarball of main `279b2235` extracted into `w/base` (dot-free), `node_modules` a symlink to the project checkout's installed modules, read-only use; the machine's load average at the first run was 37.00 12.30 5.24, so any timing is unrepresentative)
1. **RD-455 at main (plain-node probe `probe455.js`, the real validator and the real router over a real `JsonStorage` in the drafter's own folder, BASE then the applied hunks).** At main: the validator returns `INVALID_SCIM_TOKEN` for an omitted, empty, spaces-only or null token even when told a token can be kept (probe cells V1 and V2 read `refused`); a mapping-only save in scim mode with a stored token returns **400** (probe T1) and a mapping removal returns **400** (T2); the stored token is byte-equal and the issue date unchanged because the save wrote nothing. **After the hunks:** V1 and V2 read `ok` with config keys `authoritative,mode` (no token key); T1 returns **200** with the stored token byte-equal, the issue date unchanged, the mapping replaced and no token text in any response; T2 returns 200, 0 mappings, token byte-equal; controls unchanged: omitted with no stored token returns 400 `INVALID_SCIM_TOKEN` with the mode still `off` (T3); `off` then `scim` with no token returns 400 with the leftover token still stored (T4); after a revoke a mapping-only save returns 400 (T5); a stale version returns 409 `CONFIG_VERSION_CONFLICT` (T9 of the probe); a short token (V4) and non-string tokens (V5) are still refused. The audit row of a kept save reads `scimTokenConfigured` true and the token text appears in no audit payload (probe T6).
2. **RD-981 at main (plain-node probe `probe981.js`, the real `SimpleDatabase` over a real sqlite file in the drafter's own folder).** At main a 50-row list with a null first row sends **50 INSERTs** before the failure is seen (probe L1 `inserts-sent=50`) and in the drafter's first run at main's shape it left a late row behind: `rows=["x","y","q39"]` (a real leak), and in the second run at that shape (the `981-parallel` mutation, which restores main's block) it did not: `rows=["x","y"]` (the ticket's own rate is 1 to 3 in 20; two trials are the drafter's whole evidence, so no rate is claimed). A deterministic model of the late order (probe L2: every INSERT sent while another is still waiting is held and released only after the call has settled) leaves 51 rows at main (`LEAK(51 rows)`) and the pre-state after the hunk; a null at index 25 sends 50 INSERTs at main (L3) and 26 after the hunk; the controls read the same at both: a good 50-row list resolves true with 50 INSERTs, one COMMIT, no ROLLBACK and the rows in order (L4); the empty list resolves true with 0 INSERTs and one COMMIT (L5); an injected DELETE failure rejects with the original error, 0 INSERTs, one ROLLBACK and the pre-state (L6).
3. **The product hunks (frozen, `apply2139.py`, run by the drafter on a scratch copy of main's three files; `node --check` rc 0 on each).** `apply-455` printed `apply-455 entraProvisioning service 10639 -> 11809 bytes` and `apply-455 entraProvisioning route 38414 -> 39160 bytes`; `apply-981` printed `apply-981 simpleDb 30312 -> 30341 bytes`; a second `apply-455` REFUSED (rc 1); the reverts restored the three BASE blobs; `apply` (both) gave blobs `369a323801040d0e3865c66b6e428fe075beaef5` (service), `848648300444732e880df7496e78a33778204e5a` (route) and `b260b3e109e8108f2372c659dc8bc30a38cfbb99` (simpleDb). **The rule built (RD-455):** the validator takes `ctx.canKeepScimToken` (default false); in scim mode an OMITTED token (absent, null, empty or only spaces) is accepted without a token key in the config when that flag is exactly `true`, and a submitted token is always validated (a short or non-string value is refused, never read as omitted); the route computes the flag from the stored configuration (`mode === 'scim'` and a token stored: the same predicate the GET reports as `scimTokenConfigured`), writes nothing for a kept token (its existing guard `cfg.mode === 'scim' && cfg.scimBearerToken` is not met), and builds the audit summary with the stored token so the row still says one is configured. **The rule built (RD-981):** each INSERT is sent from the callback of the one before it; a failed INSERT sends the ROLLBACK and rejects from its callback (as RD-973 made it); the empty list commits the delete (the old separate branch is subsumed: `insertFrom(0)` commits when there is nothing to insert). `git diff --no-index --numstat` of main's file against the applied one printed `14 3` (service), `10 2` (route) and `15 19` (simpleDb).
